/-!
# The odd family fam(k, m), m odd, of spread-k paths: definitions and step lemmas      (S178)

`K = 2κ + 1`, `m = 2h + 1`, `k = 2κ`, `K ≥ 2m - 1` (`2h ≤ κ`).  Word `z A z B C z D` = `FamOdd.famT κ h` of length
`L = 3K + 3m + 1 = 6κ + 6h + 7` over `d = 3κ + h + 2` letters (A-letter `c ↦ c`, `n_i ↦ K + i`, `N_i ↦ K + κ + i`,
`z ↦ 3κ + h + 1`: the numbering of `pfam.fam`), down-step predicate `dn` (Sign Table of PROOF_family_odd.md) and
height function `H`.  A python twin was brute-force tested first (not included).
STATUS: everything PROVED (no `sorry`). The step lemmas `stepCA … stepDC` are in `PathFamOddStepA/B/C.lean`
(generated by a script; separate files because one file with all of them exceeds 2.2 GB).
-/

